{
  "task": "G6-051",
  "status": "in-progress",
  "scope": "Explicit opt-in signed WSS/Store/Core/RTC hosting of one duplex mono Opus audio plus one VP8 camera on local macOS arm64, two participants and real isolated Store policy. Synthetic supplied encoded source content and independent decoder; no physical camera, installed browser or complete fallback qualification.",
  "platform": "macOS-26.6.2-arm64-arm-64bit-Mach-O",
  "executed_at": "2026-10-27T14:18:09.045291+00:00",
  "source_revision_before_checkpoint": "90b0c860abd2ca9bf211ceb732bb57e1ce040e82",
  "implementation": [
    "SignalingHost retains one bounded supported mono audio codec and admits AV only when require_vp8_audio_video_profile is explicitly enabled with one exact VP8/90000/channels0/no-fmtp capability. Trickle, ambiguous/unsupported codec configuration and unbounded capacity still refuse. Default server does not install or advertise a media host.",
    "The original immutable Store offer must declare exactly one duplex logical audio stream or, for the explicit AV host, one audio and one video stream, with distinct original IDs. Actual active SDP kinds/counts/directions must match; AV requires distinct bounded MIDs. No unoffered data, duplicate media or implicit AV opt-in.",
    "Actual answer m-sections must preserve original index/kind/protocol/MID and active status with duplex direction. Audio uses the bounded actual offer/answer profile including Opus SDP /2 versus logical mono. Video uses the actual VP8/RTX profile. Per-stream answer retains each original logical ID/order and exact selected codec/rate/channels/PT. This response still grants no source readiness, media success or receive subscription.",
    "The service reserves one or two Core ports from the exact selected program, replacing the fixed audio-only capacity. Subscription selectors and early Store diagnostics use actual confirmed Audio/Video kinds, while exact original bindings and no-renegotiation checks remain. Gates can target either medium independently under their original signed lease.",
    "Core existing-port planning maps exact current direct sources onto one compatible already confirmed sink per medium, preserving distinct source and receiver IDs and original formats/directions. Source-ID unsubscribe resolves only actual installed Core routes, so a local receiver ID cannot accidentally clear a different source. Ambiguous sinks and future non-audio participant selectors refuse; the generic native resource planner is unchanged.",
    "Activated IO readiness follows original monotonic worker lifetime instead of failure to acquire a setup metadata mutex. Activation still requires installed handles after actual port readiness; a captured pre-spawn guard covers exit/drop/abort-before-first-poll. Original joins remain in setup, and late ready observations cannot resurrect cancelled workers. This metadata cannot grant media permission.",
    "Existing service answer binding, current signed scope/Endpoint/role/participant checks, original attempt identity, Core reservation/controller, physical-peer capacity and joined cleanup remain on the same paths. The AV backend is the previously guarded canonical ingress/egress/clock/repair implementation; no alternate direct media bypass."
  ],
